/**
 * The main entry point for the Flink application.
 * 
 * This method sets up a Flink StreamExecutionEnvironment, creates a data stream from a collection,
 * and executes it by adding a sink to an HBase database.
 * 
 * @param args command-line arguments (not used in this example)
 * @throws Exception if an error occurs during execution
 */
public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
    // Create a StreamExecutionEnvironment
    StreamExecutionEnvironment env = StreamExecutionEnvironment.getExecutionEnvironment();

    // Create a data stream from a collection
    DataStream<String> dataStream = env.fromElements("Hello, HBase!", "This is a test.");

    // Add a sink to an HBase database
    dataStream.addSink(new HBaseSink());

    // Execute the data stream
    env.execute("Flink HBase Example");
}
```

However, this code snippet assumes that you have already created a class named `HBaseSink` that extends `RichSinkFunction` and implements the necessary logic for writing data to an HBase database.

Here's a basic example of what the `HBaseSink` class might look like:

```java
public class HBaseSink extends RichSinkFunction<String> {
    private Connection connection;

    @Override
    public void open(Configuration parameters) throws Exception {
        // Create a connection to the HBase database
        connection = ConnectionFactory.createConnection(new Properties());
    }

    @Override
    public void close() throws Exception {
        // Close the connection to the HBase database
        if (connection != null) {
            connection.close();
        }
    }

    @Override
    public void invoke(String value, Context context) throws Exception {
        // Write the data to the HBase database
        Table table = connection.getTable("my_table");
        Put put = new Put(Bytes.toBytes("row_key"));
        put.addColumn(Bytes.toBytes("column_family"), Bytes.toBytes("column"), Bytes.toBytes(value));
        table.put(put);
        table.close();
    }
}
```

This is a very basic example and may need to be modified to suit your specific use case. You will also need to add the necessary dependencies to your project to use HBase and Flink.

